# Rust reference reader build output; Cargo.lock IS committed so CI
# resolves the same ciborium a reviewer did.
interop/rust/target/
target/release/

# local agent scratch, not part of the project
.agents/
.codex/
.claude/

# One-off probe namespaces. A reviewer or an agent with a single question
# writes one, compiles it, answers the question and forgets it -- under bench/,
# because that is the only source root a ClojureScript build already reaches.
# Seven of them once shipped in one commit (probe.cljs, probe2/probe3 and their
# mains, probe_cases, probe_fix) because somebody ran `git add -A`, and every
# review round since has left more behind: packed_probe.clj, FfmProbe.java,
# dsprobe, secprobe, probeaud, docprobe. Ignored by NAME rather than by
# discipline, since discipline is what has already failed six times.
#
# A probe that has earned a place in the repo gets a real name, a docstring
# saying which property it guards, and a bin/ci stage that runs it. Until it
# has all three it is scratch, and `git add -f` is the deliberate override.
bench/**/*probe*
bench/**/*Probe*
.fuzzscratch/
